&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a strategic Territory Sales Manager&amp;nbsp; for Japan, you will own and grow your Digital Native and Retail territory with GitLab’s enterprise relationships in the Japan market. You’ll help Enterprise organizations realize the full value of GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform by leading the entire sales cycle, from prospecting and qualification through rollout and long-term adoption. Reporting to an Area Sales Manager or Regional Director, you’ll use a consultative approach to understand complex customer needs, guide them through evaluation, and coordinate pre- and post-sales resources to ensure successful deployments and visible business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work under minimal supervision on complex deals, act as the voice of the customer into GitLab, and partner closely with our strategic channel partners to generate qualified opportunities and develop new customers. In your first year, you’ll be expected to establish and execute clear account plans for enterprise prospects and customers in the Japan market, build strong internal and external stakeholder relationships, and consistently manage your forecast and pipeline with transparency and discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support GitLab’s strategic prospects and customers in your territory in Japan&amp;nbsp; Market, with a focus in the Digital Natives and Retail industry, owning the full sales cycle for enterprise accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead account strategy by developing and executing account plans aligned to each customer’s business needs and long-term goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct prospecting and opportunity development activities in named large and strategic accounts, including working closely with strategic channel partners to generate qualified leads and new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate pre- and post-sales engagement with solutions architects, customer success, and support teams to ensure successful rollout, adoption, and expansion of GitLab products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear account leadership, including regular activity, pipeline, and forecast reporting to sales management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze wins and losses, contribute to root cause analysis, and share lessons learned with account managers, marketing, and technical teams to improve future outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer by sharing feedback and product ideas through GitLab’s public issue tracker and internal channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a consultative sales approach to uncover business issues, shape solution recommendations, and deliver compelling proposals, quotes, and presentations that address customer requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex sales cycles with large, strategic enterprise customers, selling into the Digital Natives and retail segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to prospect, qualify, and develop new opportunities while also growing existing accounts through strong account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill in leading pre- and post-sales activities, coordinating with technical, support, and channel partners to drive adoption and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in consultative selling, including uncovering business needs, building account plans, and delivering proposals and presentations that align GitLab solutions to customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prepare and maintain accurate activity, pipeline, and forecast reports, and to contribute to win/loss and root cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication and collaboration skills to share customer feedback and lessons learned with sales management, product, marketing, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software development concepts and tools, with preferred exposure to Git, software development tools, or application lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with GitLab’s values, openness to learning, and interest in applying transferable skills even if your background does not match every requirement exactly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Territory Sales Manager will join our enterprise sales team, which focuses on driving GitLab adoption with large customers in the Japan market. The team is responsible for the full relationship lifecycle with enterprise accounts, from initial engagement through long-term expansion and advocacy, ensuring customers realize value from GitLab’s DevSecOps platform. Team members work in an all-remote, distributed environment and collaborate asynchronously across time zones with sales leadership, solutions architects, customer success, marketing, and channel partners. The team is currently focused on maintaining and growing our existing footprint in the region, executing a consistent global sales motion while adapting to local customer needs and partnering closely with strategic channel organizations to reach and support key accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional details about our process can be found on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;hiring page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_actions__container c-message__actions&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: xx-small;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;Remote-Global&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Axon and be a Force for Good.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Axon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Axon’s mission is simple and bold: &lt;strong&gt;Protect Life&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build technology that helps first responders, security teams, and communities act with speed, clarity, and confidence in the moments that matter most. Our Real-Time Operations (RTO) portfolio, anchored by the Fusus platform, is transforming how law enforcement, enterprise security, and international agencies detect, assess, and respond to threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fusus connects live video, alerts, sensors, and location data into a unified operating picture, accessible on any device. Alerts and presence are the heartbeat of that picture. They determine what demands attention and who is in position to act. We&#39;re building intelligent, high-signal alerting and presence experiences that cut through noise and keep operators and responders locked into what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Manager for Alerts &amp;amp; Presence, you will define and lead the roadmap for how Fusus surfaces the right information to the right people at the right time - making alerts and responder presence the connective tissue of real-time operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll build the systems that determine what warrants attention, how it&#39;s prioritized and routed, and how operators maintain awareness of who is where. This spans alert generation from cameras, sensors, LPR, drones, and third-party sources, as well as the presence layer that tracks responder locations, unit status, and asset proximity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will enable officers, security teams, and emergency responders around the world to cut through noise, act on what matters, and coordinate with confidence. By making alerts smarter and presence data seamless, your work will help prevent harm, accelerate response, and directly advance Axon&#39;s mission to Protect Life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Alerts &amp;amp; Presence product roadmap, focused on delivering the right information at the right time to operators and responders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how alerts are generated, prioritized, routed, and resolved across video, sensors, LPR, drones, and third-party integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build presence experiences that give operators real-time visibility into responder locations, unit status, and asset proximity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design fast, intuitive workflows for monitoring incidents, triaging alerts, and coordinating response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and design to ship responsive, low-latency, and reliable alerting and presence features across web and mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage global law enforcement and enterprise users to validate needs and test improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with other product teams to ensure alerts and presence data flow seamlessly across the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use metrics and feedback to refine roadmap priorities - reducing alert fatigue, improving time-to-action, and increasing situational awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support go-to-market, training, and rollout with cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operators and responders receive timely, high-signal alerts that drive faster, more confident decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presence data gives commanders and dispatchers clear visibility into who is where - improving coordination and resource deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adoption grows across customer segments with high daily use, strong retention, and positive field feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every second saved contributes to safer outcomes for officers, teams, and the public&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–8+ years of product management experience, including 3+ years working on real-time, event-driven, or alerting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products where speed, clarity, and reliability directly impact outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of alerting frameworks, geolocation and presence systems, real-time data pipelines, and notification design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with live video, sensor networks, LPR, drone telemetry, and IoT integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of turning user insights into clear product direction and focused execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead cross-functional teams through roadmap, design, delivery, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator who drives alignment, decisions, and measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Axon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the future of public-private security collaboration, creating safer outcomes for communities and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a mission-driven company with a history of innovation and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside passionate teams building technology that protects lives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits that Benefit You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary and RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan with matching contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private health insurance and cash plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 days paid holiday plus UK public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity and paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GymPass subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance and income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth, learning support, and wellness resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement? That&#39;s ok. At Axon, we Aim Far. We think big with a long-term view because we want to reinvent the world to be a safer, better place. We are also committed to building diverse teams that reflect the communities we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they check every box in the job description. If you’re excited about this role and our mission to Protect Life but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification listed here, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above job description is not intended as, nor should it be construed as, exhaustive of all duties, responsibilities, skills, efforts, or working conditions associated with this job. The job description may change or be supplemented at any time in accordance with business needs and conditions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Some roles may also require legal eligibility to work in a firearms environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We collect personal information from applicants to evaluate candidates for employment. You may request access, deletion, or exercise other CCPA rights at&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; ----- target=&quot;_blank&quot; ----- ----- via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://privacyportal.onetrust.com/webform/0efc1702-9321-4119-bc9d-a06c3a1d3e4e/ca57cc26-a159-4193-9f6e-58ffe3fd2509&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://privacyportal.onetrust.com/webform/0efc1702-9321-4119-bc9d-a06c3a1d3e4e/ca57cc26-a159-4193-9f6e-58ffe3fd2509&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Axon Privacy Web Form&lt;/a&gt;. For more information, please see the Your California Privacy Rights section of our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.axon.com/candidateprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.axon.com/candidateprivacypolicy&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Axon’s mission is to Protect Life and is committed to the well-being and safety of its employees as well as Axon’s impact on the environment. All Axon employees must be aware of and committed to the appropriate environmental, health, and safety regulations, policies, and procedures. Axon employees are empowered to report safety concerns as they arise and activities potentially impacting the environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer that promotes justice, advances equity, values diversity and fosters inclusion. We’re committed to hiring the best talent — regardless of race, creed, color, ancestry, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship status, marital status, disability, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances — and empowering all of our employees so they can do their best work. If you have a disability or special need that requires assistance or accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please email &lt;a ---------- &lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;Please note that this email address is for accommodation purposes only. Axon will not respond to inquiries for other purposes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
