&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or a related IT discipline; or equivalent professional experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Technical Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in Software QA, including functional, system, API, and integration testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience with automation tools and frameworks i.e. Playwright &amp;amp; TestIM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;CRM&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;ERP&lt;/strong&gt; domain knowledge i.e. Salesforce, Zuora, NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Salesforce platform including CPQ, Sales process, Lightning and Salesforce integration with other tools/systems using API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Java, Javascript and XPath identification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in using AI tools like&lt;strong&gt; Claude&lt;/strong&gt; for building agents for QA workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Enterprise Applications QA Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Applications QA Team at GitLab is a dynamic, cross-functional group dedicated to the quality of all the business applications. Focusing on both CRM systems and Finance systems, the team authors and maintains the manual and automated test suites. The team owns the execution of test cycles to confirm the defect-free release of the applications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
